silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_04_negative_witnesses_concrete_anchor_4#negativewitnessshortcutsource silm:hasLongDescription "The NegativeWitnessShortcutSource is The lower-row occurrence of NegativeWitness is the source of the dashed-red shortcut not-exists direct. For the catus-collision probe, this anchors the candidate \"bare catus row\" attempting to bypass type and gate_refuse and assert directly into the negative-witness apex. The duplicate cell makes the shortcut visually nameable; the dashed red rendering signals refusal status. Without the duplicate cell, the diagram could not exhibit the forbidden route as a positioned arrow." .
